gametitle=Madden NFL 2004 (SLUS-20752, CRC 14F8B841)
comment=State-47 lead-blocker steering candidates -- enable ONE block at a time

// ===========================================================================
// PURPOSE
//
// The pulling guard on the misdirection play commits his block ~0.5 yd past
// the line (metric lead_blocker_block_depth) and the run stuffs for ~1 yd
// (metric carrier_yards). The goal: make him pull PAST the first man and
// engage a linebacker/safety at the second level, so the play breaks bigger.
//
// These patch the state-47 steering only (0x001B61A0), which fb-wr-blocking.md
// established is the lead blocker's OWN targeting -- he is excluded from the
// general assignment system, so changing this touches only lead blockers and
// not ordinary line play.
//
// HOW TO USE
//
//   0. This is a reference sheet, not the loaded file. PenguinScreen2 loads
//      ONE pnach per game by CRC name: ~/.config/PenguinScreen2/patches/
//      14F8B841.pnach, with EnablePatches=true (already set on the rig). So a
//      candidate only runs when its lines are inside THAT file, alongside the
//      DNAS bypass from patches/14F8B841.pnach in the repo.
//   1. It must be a CODE patch, so it goes through pnach, not a PINE write:
//      PCSX2's EE recompiler caches compiled blocks and ignores a bare RAM
//      write (docs/lab-design.md, 2026-08-11). pnach patch=1 lines apply on a
//      path that invalidates the recompiler.
//   2. Assemble the active file: copy the DNAS bypass block from
//      patches/14F8B841.pnach, append exactly ONE candidate block below with
//      its `//` removed, and place the result at
//      ~/.config/PenguinScreen2/patches/14F8B841.pnach on the rig.
//   3. Reboot PenguinScreen2 (patches apply at boot), get to the misdirection
//      play, save a mid-play pre-snap state to a scratch slot (6+).
//   4. Measure: python -m tools.madden_lab trial --spec experiments/lead_blocker.py
//      and compare carrier_yards / lead_blocker_block_depth to the ~0.95 / ~0.55
//      baseline.
//   5. Next candidate: re-assemble, reboot, re-save, measure.
//
// Every patched word below was decoded back to the intended instruction before
// being written here; the "was:" note is the shipped word.
//
// THE STEERING, for reference (disassembled 0x001B61A0):
//   0x001B61A4/AC  lui a2,0x002a / ori a2,0xaaaa   cone half-angle = 60 deg
//   0x001B61E8     lui at,0x4060 -> f20            search + commit distance 3.5
//   0x001B6234     lui at,0x3fe0 -> f20            tighter commit 1.75 (opp arm)
//   0x001B6284     add.s f1,f1,f0                  apply 2x velocity lead, X
//   0x001B6294     add.s f2,f2,f0                  apply 2x velocity lead, Y
//   0x001B623C     c.lt.s f0,f20                   commit when nearer than f20
// ===========================================================================


// --- Candidate 1 -- NARROW the target cone, 60 deg -> 25 deg ----------------
// Hypothesis: the near down-lineman sits off to the side; the second-level
// defender is straighter ahead in the pull lane. A tighter cone should skip
// the side man and select the one downfield.  (was: 3c06002a / 34c6aaaa)
//patch=1,EE,001B61A4,word,3C060011
//patch=1,EE,001B61AC,word,34C6C71C


// --- Candidate 2 -- WIDEN the target cone, 60 deg -> 100 deg -----------------
// Hypothesis: the opposite -- a wider cone lets the finder consider a deeper
// defender it currently cannot see, if selection favours alignment over range.
// (was: 3c06002a / 34c6aaaa)
//patch=1,EE,001B61A4,word,3C060047
//patch=1,EE,001B61AC,word,34C61C71


// --- Candidate 3 -- LARGER search/commit distance, 3.5 -> 6.0 ----------------
// Hypothesis: the finder reaches a defender further away, letting the guard
// lock onto a second-level man before the near one is in range. f20 feeds both
// the cone-finder range and the same-arm commit test.  (was: 3c014060)
//patch=1,EE,001B61E8,word,3C0140C0


// --- Candidate 4 -- SMALLER commit distance, 3.5 -> 2.0 ----------------------
// Hypothesis: he keeps steering his route until much closer, so he drifts
// past the line before the commit test passes and he engages deeper.
// (was: 3c014060)
//patch=1,EE,001B61E8,word,3C014000


// --- Candidate 5 -- widen the tighter opponent-commit gate, 1.75 -> 3.0 ------
// The second commit test (0x001B6234) governs an un-engaged opponent target.
// Raising it lets him accept that target from further out -- pairs naturally
// with a cone change.  (was: 3c013fe0)
//patch=1,EE,001B6234,word,3C014040


// --- Candidate 6 -- REMOVE the 2x velocity lead (aim at current position) ----
// Control / diagnostic. He currently aims at target + 2x velocity; nop-ing
// both lead adds makes him aim at the defender's present spot. If block depth
// moves, the lead is what is pulling his engagement forward.  (was:
// 46000840 at 6284, 46001080 at 6294)
//patch=1,EE,001B6284,word,00000000
//patch=1,EE,001B6294,word,00000000


// --- Candidate 7 -- AMPLIFY the downfield lead only (Y: posY + 2vY -> 4vY) ---
// Doubles the Y (downfield) lead by feeding the already-doubled 2*velY back
// through the position add twice is not a one-word change; instead this routes
// the X-lead slot's doubled value is not reusable -- so this candidate is left
// as a NOTE, not a patch: amplifying the lead cleanly needs a cave routine,
// which is deferred until an in-place candidate is shown to move the metric.
